WEBVTT

00:00:01.300 --> 00:00:02.800
Hi, Pinky here!

00:00:03.320 --> 00:00:06.160
Quick one. If you double the sides of a square,

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:07.780
how much bigger is the area?

00:00:08.440 --> 00:00:10.380
Most people's gut says double.

00:00:10.820 --> 00:00:11.720
Let's see.

00:00:12.960 --> 00:00:14.540
Here's a square with side three.

00:00:14.980 --> 00:00:16.500
Its area is three squared:

00:00:16.800 --> 00:00:19.260
nine. Now double every side.

00:00:19.720 --> 00:00:22.440
Side six. Six squared is thirty-six.

00:00:23.280 --> 00:00:26.020
Thirty-six is not two times nine.

00:00:26.280 --> 00:00:27.860
It's four times nine.

00:00:28.280 --> 00:00:31.800
Look. Four copies of the little square fit inside the big

00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:32.700
one.

00:00:34.380 --> 00:00:35.300
That's the rule.

00:00:35.840 --> 00:00:37.760
If lengths get multiplied by k,

00:00:38.460 --> 00:00:40.560
area gets multiplied by k squared.

00:00:42.600 --> 00:00:45.520
Your turn. A shape has an area of five.

00:00:46.040 --> 00:00:48.200
Make every length three times as long.

00:00:48.760 --> 00:00:49.660
What's the new area?

00:00:50.160 --> 00:00:51.060
Go.

00:00:57.340 --> 00:00:59.280
Forty-five! Three squared is nine.

00:00:59.660 --> 00:01:00.560
Nine times five.

00:01:02.240 --> 00:01:04.000
This is the fast way,

00:01:04.200 --> 00:01:06.520
because you don't have to recalculate every side.

00:01:06.900 --> 00:01:08.080
Just find the scale factor.

00:01:09.920 --> 00:01:11.740
It even works in three dimensions.

00:01:12.380 --> 00:01:14.780
Volume scales by the cube of the length factor.

00:01:15.240 --> 00:01:16.360
Double the sides of a cube,

00:01:16.640 --> 00:01:18.320
and you get eight times the volume.

00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:22.920
One condition. The shapes have to be similar.

00:01:23.520 --> 00:01:25.900
Every matching length scaled by the same amount.

00:01:26.300 --> 00:01:27.440
Stretch just one side,

00:01:27.440 --> 00:01:28.760
and this rule is off.

00:01:30.880 --> 00:01:31.880
And watch your units.

00:01:32.540 --> 00:01:33.440
Plain units for length.

00:01:34.020 --> 00:01:35.280
Square units for area.

00:01:35.840 --> 00:01:36.880
Cubic units for volume.

00:01:37.380 --> 00:01:38.920
Now hit Try this skill,

00:01:38.920 --> 00:01:40.220
and go scale something!
